<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>One step of the L
<div id="S3.F2.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:7.5pt;height:6.8pt;vertical-align:-6.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:7.5pt;transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) rotate(-180deg) ;">
<p id="S3.F2.4.1" class="ltx_p">A</p>
</span></div>TINO solver, a discretization of the Langevin SDE (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>) which targets the posterior <math id="S3.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}|{\bm{y}},c,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}|{\bm{y}},c,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, involving two stochastic autoencoding (SAE) steps and two proximal steps.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Under mild regularity assumptions on <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{V}({\bm{x}}|c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{V}({\bm{x}}|c)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{I}({\bm{x}}|c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{I}({\bm{x}}|c)</annotation></semantics></math>, starting from an initial condition <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the process <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to a <math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of <math id="S3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}|{\bm{y}},c,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}|{\bm{y}},c,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> exponentially fast as <math id="S3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laumont et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. While solving (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3 L A TINO for High Definition video posterior sampling ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) exactly is not possible, considering numerical approximations of <math id="S3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> provides a powerful computational framework for deriving approximate samplers for <math id="S3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}|{\bm{y}},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}|{\bm{y}},c)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">L
<span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:7.5pt;height:6.8pt;vertical-align:-6.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:7.5pt;transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) rotate(-180deg) ;">
<span id="S3.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">A</span>
</span></span>TINO  stems from approximating (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3 L A TINO for High Definition video posterior sampling ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) by a Markov chain derived from the following recursion: given an initialization <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a step-size <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}={\bm{x}}_{k}+\!\!\int_{0}^{\delta}\!\!\eta\nabla\log p_{V}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{s}|c)\mathrm{d}s+\sqrt{2\eta}\,\mathrm{d}\bm{w}_{s},\quad\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{0}={\bm{x}}_{k}}_{\text{VCM prior step}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.660em;" width="0.660em"><mo>+</mo></mpadded><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></msup><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒘</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>VCM prior step</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}={\bm{x}}_{k}+\!\!\int_{0}^{\delta}\!\!\eta\nabla\log p_{V}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{s}|c)\mathrm{d}s+\sqrt{2\eta}\,\mathrm{d}\bm{w}_{s},\quad\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{0}={\bm{x}}_{k}}_{\text{VCM prior step}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}={\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}+\eta\delta\nabla\log p\left({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}\right)+\eta\delta\nabla\log\tilde{p}_{\gamma\phi}\left({\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}|\lambda\right)}_{\text{implicit likelihood half-step with $\phi$-regularization}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>implicit likelihood half-step with </mtext><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mtext>-regularization</mtext></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}={\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}+\eta\delta\nabla\log p\left({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}\right)+\eta\delta\nabla\log\tilde{p}_{\gamma\phi}\left({\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}|\lambda\right)}_{\text{implicit likelihood half-step with $\phi$-regularization}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}={\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}+\!\!\int_{0}^{\delta}\!\!{(1-\eta)}\nabla\log p_{I}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{s}|c)\mathrm{d}s+\sqrt{2(1-\eta)}\,\mathrm{d}\bm{w}_{s},\quad\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{0}={\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}}_{\text{ICM prior step}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mpadded style="width:0.660em;" width="0.660em"><mo>+</mo></mpadded><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>I</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒘</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>ICM prior step</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}={\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}+\!\!\int_{0}^{\delta}\!\!{(1-\eta)}\nabla\log p_{I}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{s}|c)\mathrm{d}s+\sqrt{2(1-\eta)}\,\mathrm{d}\bm{w}_{s},\quad\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{0}={\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}}_{\text{ICM prior step}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{{\bm{x}}_{k+1}={\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}+(1-\eta)\delta\nabla\log p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}}_{k+1})}_{\text{implicit likelihood half-step}}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>implicit likelihood half-step</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{{\bm{x}}_{k+1}={\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}+(1-\eta)\delta\nabla\log p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}}_{k+1})}_{\text{implicit likelihood half-step}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where we identify a splitting in which each CM prior is involved separately through exact integration (these integrals will be approximated through SAE steps), and the likelihood is involved through two implicit (backward Euler) half-steps. Importantly, unlike the explicit steps used in most Langevin sampling algorithms, the implicit steps in (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>) remain numerically stable for all <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This allows L
<span id="S3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:7.5pt;height:6.8pt;vertical-align:-6.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:7.5pt;transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) rotate(-180deg) ;">
<span id="S3.p6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A</span>
</span></span>TINO  to converge quickly by taking <math id="S3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> large, albeit with some small bias. Conversely, the widely used unadjusted Langevin algorithm (ULA) integrates only the Brownian term <math id="S3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{w}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{w}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> exactly, it involves gradients via an explicit Euler step, and is explosive unless <math id="S3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently small. It is worth recalling that the Langevin diffusion is a time-homogeneous process. The iterates <math id="S3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> resulting from its discrete-time approximation are asymptotically ergodic, converging to a neighborhood of <math id="S3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p({\bm{x}}|{\bm{y}},c,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{x}}|{\bm{y}},c,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Unlike DMs, these iterates do not travel backwards in time through an inhomogeneous process. Therefore, Langevin algorithms use directly the likelihood <math id="S3.p6.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})\propto\exp{\{-\|{\bm{y}}-\mathcal{A}{\bm{x}}\|_{2}^{2}/2\sigma_{n}^{2}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})\propto\exp{\{-\|{\bm{y}}-\mathcal{A}{\bm{x}}\|_{2}^{2}/2\sigma_{n}^{2}\}}</annotation></semantics></math>, avoiding the need to approximate the likelihood of <math id="S3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. a noisy version of <math id="S3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as required in guided DMs like <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chung et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2023a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Spagnoletti et al. (2025)</a></cite>, we compute <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}</annotation></semantics></math> approximately via SAE steps,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{D}^{V}\left(f^{V}_{\vartheta}\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t^{(V)}_{k}}}\mathcal{E}_{V}\big({\bm{x}}^{(k)}\big)+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t^{(V)}_{k}}}\bm{\epsilon},{t}^{(V)}_{k}\right),c\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{D}^{V}\left(f^{V}_{\vartheta}\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t^{(V)}_{k}}}\mathcal{E}_{V}\big({\bm{x}}^{(k)}\big)+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t^{(V)}_{k}}}\bm{\epsilon},{t}^{(V)}_{k}\right),c\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{x}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{D}^{I}\left(f^{I}_{\theta}\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{{t}^{(I)}_{k}}}\mathcal{E}_{I}\big({\bm{x}}^{(k)}\big)+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t^{(I)}_{k}}}\bm{\epsilon},t^{(I)}_{k},c\right)\right)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{D}^{I}\left(f^{I}_{\theta}\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{{t}^{(I)}_{k}}}\mathcal{E}_{I}\big({\bm{x}}^{(k)}\big)+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t^{(I)}_{k}}}\bm{\epsilon},t^{(I)}_{k},c\right)\right)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">where we recall that <math id="S3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{E}^{I},\mathcal{D}^{I},f^{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{E}^{I},\mathcal{D}^{I},f^{I})</annotation></semantics></math> act frame-wise and that <math id="S3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{V}_{\vartheta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{V}_{\vartheta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{I}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{I}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> have model-specific schedules.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The implicit Euler steps in (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>) can be reformulated as an explicit proximal point steps as follows</p>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}=&amp;\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\left(\inf_{{\bm{u}}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}}\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}}^{\prime})+\tfrac{1}{2\gamma}\|{\bm{u}}-{\bm{u}}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\right)+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}\,,\\
\approx&amp;\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}\,,\\
\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+1}=&amp;\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta(1-\eta)}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}\,,\\
\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝐲</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≈</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝐲</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝐲</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}=&amp;\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\left(\inf_{{\bm{u}}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}}\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}}^{\prime})+\tfrac{1}{2\gamma}\|{\bm{u}}-{\bm{u}}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}\right)+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}\,,\\
\approx&amp;\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}\,,\\
\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+1}=&amp;\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta(1-\eta)}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}\,,\\
\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\bm{y}}:{\bm{x}}\mapsto-\log p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\bm{y}}:{\bm{x}}\mapsto-\log p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and where we have simplified the computation of <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by assuming that <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\ll\delta\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\ll\delta\eta</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pereyra, 2016</a>)</cite>. The optimization problems described above are strongly convex and can be efficiently approximated by using a small number of iterations of a specialized solver. In particular, to compute <math id="S3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we employ a few iterations of the conjugate gradient algorithm with warm-starting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hestenes &amp; Stiefel, 1952</a>)</cite>. For the computation of <math id="S3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we recommend using a proximal splitting optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chambolle &amp; Pock, 2011</a>)</cite>, or a warm-started Adam optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma &amp; Ba, 2014</a>)</cite>, both of which are effective in practice. Please see Appendix <a href="#A1.SS5" title="A.5 Ablation study ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> for more details.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Refer to Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 L A TINO for High Definition video posterior sampling ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for more details about L
<span id="S3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:7.5pt;height:6.8pt;vertical-align:-6.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:7.5pt;transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) rotate(-180deg) ;">
<span id="S3.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">A</span>
</span></span>TINO, and to Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3 L A TINO for High Definition video posterior sampling ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> for its schematic representation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> L
<div id="alg1.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:7.5pt;height:6.8pt;vertical-align:-6.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:7.5pt;transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) rotate(-180deg) ;">
<p id="alg1.5.1" class="ltx_p">A</p>
</span></div>TINO (LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">given</span> degraded video <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, operator <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, initialization <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}=\mathcal{A}^{\dagger}{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}=\mathcal{A}^{\dagger}{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, video lenght <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T+1</annotation></semantics></math>, steps <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=5</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">given</span> video CM <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{E}_{V},\mathcal{D}_{V},f^{V}_{\vartheta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{E}_{V},\mathcal{D}_{V},f^{V}_{\vartheta})</annotation></semantics></math>, image CM <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{E}_{I},\mathcal{D}_{I},f^{I}_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{E}_{I},\mathcal{D}_{I},f^{I}_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, schedules <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t^{(V)}_{k},t^{(I)}_{k},\delta_{k},\eta,\lambda\}_{k=0}^{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t^{(V)}_{k},t^{(I)}_{k},\delta_{k},\eta,\lambda\}_{k=0}^{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,\ldots,N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,\ldots,N-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"># VCM prior half-step (temporal coherence)</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{V}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\big(0,{\mathrm{Id}}_{(1+T/4)\times H/8\times W/8\times C}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{V}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\big(0,{\mathrm{Id}}_{(1+T/4)\times H/8\times W/8\times C}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}^{(V)}_{t^{(V)}_{k}}\leftarrow\sqrt{\alpha_{t^{(V)}_{k}}}\;\mathcal{E}_{V}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{k-1}\big)\;+\;\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t^{(V)}_{k}}}\;\bm{\epsilon}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}^{(V)}_{t^{(V)}_{k}}\leftarrow\sqrt{\alpha_{t^{(V)}_{k}}}\;\mathcal{E}_{V}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{k-1}\big)\;+\;\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t^{(V)}_{k}}}\;\bm{\epsilon}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{V}\!\big(f^{V}_{\vartheta}({\bm{z}}^{(V)}_{t^{(V)}_{k}},\,t^{(V)}_{k})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>ϑ</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{V}\!\big(f^{V}_{\vartheta}({\bm{z}}^{(V)}_{t^{(V)}_{k}},\,t^{(V)}_{k})\big)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> VCM
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"># First likelihood - Solved with proximal splitting or Adam iterations</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}\leftarrow\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}}g_{y}({\bm{u}})+\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta_{k}\eta}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}\leftarrow\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}}g_{y}({\bm{u}})+\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta_{k}\eta}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"># ICM prior half-step (per-frame detail)</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{I}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\big(0,{\mathrm{Id}}_{h/8\times w/8\times c}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{I}\sim\mathcal{N}\!\big(0,{\mathrm{Id}}_{h/8\times w/8\times c}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}\leftarrow\mathrm{stack}_{\tau=0}^{T}\;\mathcal{D}_{I}\!\Big(f^{I}_{\theta}\big(\sqrt{\alpha_{t^{(I)}_{k}}}\;\mathcal{E}_{I}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}},\tau})+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t^{(I)}_{k}}}\;\bm{\epsilon}_{I},\;t^{(I)}_{k}\big)\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>stack</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}\leftarrow\mathrm{stack}_{\tau=0}^{T}\;\mathcal{D}_{I}\!\Big(f^{I}_{\theta}\big(\sqrt{\alpha_{t^{(I)}_{k}}}\;\mathcal{E}_{I}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}},\tau})+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t^{(I)}_{k}}}\;\bm{\epsilon}_{I},\;t^{(I)}_{k}\big)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> ICM
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"># Likelihood prox (2nd) - Solved with conjugate gradient iterations</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{k}\leftarrow\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}}g_{y}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta_{k}(1-\eta)}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{k}\leftarrow\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}}g_{y}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta_{k}(1-\eta)}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"># Final iteration: skip ICM and second likelihood</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{k}\leftarrow\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{k}\leftarrow\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement L
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:7.5pt;height:6.8pt;vertical-align:-6.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:7.5pt;transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) rotate(-180deg) ;">
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">A</span>
</span></span>TINO by using <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CausVid</span> as VCM prior. We adopt the standard bidirectional WaN architecture, fine-tuned as a CM. The model also supports an autoregressive configuration, which we do not utilize here, leaving the exploration of autoregressive priors for longer video restoration to future work. Concerning the ICM, we use <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DMD2</span>, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Spagnoletti et al. (2025)</a></cite>. For our experiments, we use <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{(V)}\in\{757,522,375,255,125\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>757,522,375,255,125</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{(V)}\in\{757,522,375,255,125\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{(I)}\in\{374,249,124,63\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>374,249,124</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>63</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{(I)}\in\{374,249,124,63\}</annotation></semantics></math> for the VCM and ICM respectively. This results in a total of 9 NFEs, where applying the ICM across all frames counts as a single NFE. Regarding the text prompt specifying VCM and ICM, in the same spirit as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon &amp; Ye (2025b)</a></cite>, we do not perform any prompt optimization and instead use the generic prompt <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">“A high resolution video/image”</em>. Exploring prompt optimization by leveraging the maximum likelihood strategy of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Spagnoletti et al. (2025)</a></cite> remains a key direction for future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset and Metrics.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate our methods on the <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Adobe240</span> dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, which contains high-quality, high-frame-rate video sequences.
From the full dataset we extract <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="435" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>435</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">435</annotation></semantics></math> video clips of <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25</annotation></semantics></math> frames each, and rescale them to a spatial resolution of <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1280\times 768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1280</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1280\times 768</annotation></semantics></math> pixels to match the high-resolution regime targeted by our method.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We assess reconstruction quality using peak signal-to-noise ratio (PSNR) and structural similarity index (SSIM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2004</a>)</cite>. Additionally, we evaluate two perceptual metrics: Learned Perceptual Image Patch Similarity (LPIPS) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, along with the recently proposed Fréchet Video Motion Distance (FVMD) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> which is tailored for assessing motion smoothness and perceptual quality in videos.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inverse Problems.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider three linear inverse problems for high-resolution video restoration. Let <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}=({\bm{x}}_{\tau})_{\tau=0}^{T}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}=({\bm{x}}_{\tau})_{\tau=0}^{T}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times C}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the unknown high-resolution video and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}=\mathcal{A}{\bm{x}}+{\bm{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝒏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}=\mathcal{A}{\bm{x}}+{\bm{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> the observed degraded video with additive Gaussian noise <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For fair comparisons, we consider a mild noise regime <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}=0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}=0.001</annotation></semantics></math>, which addresses the noiseless case.</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem A</span> - <em id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Temporal SR<math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> SR<math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 4</annotation></semantics></math>:</em> here <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> first applies temporal average pooling with factor <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> (reducing the frame rate), followed by frame-wise spatial downsampling by factor <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, simulating a low frame rate and low resolution video.
<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                    
                    
                    
                  Temporal SR<math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>k is also a coarse (Riemann sum) approximation of motion blur due to moving objects or camera during full continuous exposure between frames <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.</span></span></span>
Temporal upsampling to generate the missing frame is highly challenging here, as it requires prior knowledge of motion.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem B</span> - <em id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Temporal blur <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> SR<math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 8</annotation></semantics></math>:</em> here <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> first applies a uniform blur kernel of size <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math> pixels along the temporal dimension, followed by frame-wise spatial downsampling by a factor <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>,
simulating a motion-blurred and low-resolution video <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon &amp; Ye, 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon &amp; Ye, 2025b</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem C</span> - <em id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Temporal SR<math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 8</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> SR<math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 8</annotation></semantics></math>:</em> is a harder version of <span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem A</span>, where <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> first applies temporal average pooling with factor <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> and then a spatial downsampling by factor <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:30.7pt;vertical-align:-14.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-199.8pt,15.4pt) scale(0.498641223618483,0.498641223618483) ;">
<table id="S4.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
