<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Implementation of the forward operators</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all the inverse problems considered, we use the following formulation</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\texttt{SpatialSR}\circ\texttt{TemporalSR}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">SpatialSR</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">TemporalSR</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\texttt{SpatialSR}\circ\texttt{TemporalSR}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For <em id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Temporal SR<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> + Spatial SR<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 4</annotation></semantics></math></em>, we apply a temporal average pooling with factor <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> (with end padding if <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is not divisible),
followed by frame-wise spatial downsampling with factor <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DeepInv.Downsampling</span>  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tachella et al. (2025)</a></cite>).
The adjoint <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> first applies the spatial adjoint
(back-projection to HR) and then the adjoint of temporal averaging (nearest upsample by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> divided by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, with folding of the padded tail back to the last frame when <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is not a multiple of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>). The same approach, but with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 8</annotation></semantics></math>, is adopted for the <em id="A1.SS1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Temporal SR<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 8</annotation></semantics></math> + Spatial SR<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 8</annotation></semantics></math></em> problem.
For the <em id="A1.SS1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Temporal blur + Spatial SR<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 8</annotation></semantics></math></em> task, we use a 1D temporal uniform convolution with circular boundary conditions via FFT of window size of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>, followed by frame-wise spatial downsampling with factor <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>; the adjoint corresponds to spatial back-projection and time-reversed temporal filtering via FFT.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Implementation of Likelihood Proximal Steps</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will now describe the implementation of the likelihood updates in the splitting scheme (Equation(<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>)) instantiated by task-specific linear operators <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> over videos <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math>. We remind that we have to solve the following problems:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝐲</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">and</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta(1-\eta)}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝐲</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\argmin_{{\bm{u}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(T+1)\times H\times W\times 3}}g_{\bm{y}}({\bm{u}})+\tfrac{1}{2\delta(1-\eta)}\|\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{3}}{{4}}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{\bm{y}}(\cdot)=\tfrac{1}{2\sigma_{n}^{2}}\|\mathcal{A}\cdot-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\bm{y}}(\cdot)=\tfrac{1}{2\sigma_{n}^{2}}\|\mathcal{A}\cdot-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Starting from Equation (<a href="#A1.E9" title="In A.2 Implementation of Likelihood Proximal Steps ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), we notice that this is exactly the shape of the <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{prox}_{\nicefrac{{\delta(1-\eta)}}{{2}}\|\mathcal{A}\cdot-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}}({\bm{u}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mi mathsize="0.710em">δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.710em" minsize="0.710em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">η</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.710em" minsize="0.710em">)</mo></mrow></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{prox}_{\nicefrac{{\delta(1-\eta)}}{{2}}\|\mathcal{A}\cdot-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}}({\bm{u}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we thus provide details about the computation of this step.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Quadratic proximal (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> data term).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (which may include <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\eta</annotation></semantics></math> as well as the noise variance <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>), the quadratic likelihood proximal operator</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{prox}_{\frac{\epsilon}{2}\|\mathcal{A}\,\cdot-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}}({\bm{u}})=\arg\min_{{\bm{x}}}\tfrac{\epsilon}{2}\|\mathcal{A}{\bm{x}}-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></munder><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{prox}_{\frac{\epsilon}{2}\|\mathcal{A}\,\cdot-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}}({\bm{u}})=\arg\min_{{\bm{x}}}\tfrac{\epsilon}{2}\|\mathcal{A}{\bm{x}}-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{u}}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">reduces to the normal equations</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big({\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\,\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}\big)\,{\bm{x}}\;=\;{\bm{u}}+\epsilon\,\mathcal{A}^{\top}{\bm{y}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big({\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\,\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}\big)\,{\bm{x}}\;=\;{\bm{u}}+\epsilon\,\mathcal{A}^{\top}{\bm{y}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathrm{Id}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Id</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathrm{Id}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity operator.
The exact solution is computationally tractable in high dimensions when <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a closed-form and fast SVD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2020</a>)</cite><span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
                
                
                
              For <span id="footnote4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problems A, B, C</span>, the SVD of <math id="footnote4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed in terms of Fourier transforms, only if convolutions are periodic, which is not always the case for the kind of spatial and temporal blur we have in our case.</span></span></span>,
but to make our method applicable to general operators, we solve this linear system approximately using <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 10</annotation></semantics></math>
<em id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Conjugate Gradient</em> (CG) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hestenes &amp; Stiefel, 1952</a>)</cite> iterations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">CG is a Krylov-subspace method that iteratively refines an approximate solution
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> without explicitly inverting <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Starting from the initial guess <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}^{(0)}={\bm{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}^{(0)}={\bm{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we iteratively update:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{r}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{r}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{b}}-\big({\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}\big){\bm{x}}^{(k)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{b}}-\big({\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}\big){\bm{x}}^{(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{b}}:={\bm{u}}+\epsilon\,\mathcal{A}^{\top}{\bm{y}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{b}}:={\bm{u}}+\epsilon\,\mathcal{A}^{\top}{\bm{y}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{p}}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{p}}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{r}}^{(k)}+\beta^{(k)}{\bm{p}}^{(k-1)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{r}}^{(k)}+\beta^{(k)}{\bm{p}}^{(k-1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta^{(k)}:=\frac{\|{\bm{r}}^{(k)}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|{\bm{r}}^{(k-1)}\|_{2}^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta^{(k)}:=\frac{\|{\bm{r}}^{(k)}\|_{2}^{2}}{\|{\bm{r}}^{(k-1)}\|_{2}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\|{\bm{r}}^{(k)}\|_{2}^{2}}{\langle{\bm{p}}^{(k)},\,({\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}){\bm{p}}^{(k)}\rangle}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\|{\bm{r}}^{(k)}\|_{2}^{2}}{\langle{\bm{p}}^{(k)},\,({\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}){\bm{p}}^{(k)}\rangle},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{x}}^{(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{x}}^{(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{x}}^{(k)}+\alpha^{(k)}{\bm{p}}^{(k)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{x}}^{(k)}+\alpha^{(k)}{\bm{p}}^{(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{r}}^{(k+1)}={\bm{r}}^{(k)}-\alpha^{(k)}\big({\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}\big){\bm{p}}^{(k)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{r}}^{(k+1)}={\bm{r}}^{(k)}-\alpha^{(k)}\big({\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}\big){\bm{p}}^{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The algorithm terminates after a fixed number of iterations or once the residual norm <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{r}}^{(k)}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{r}}^{(k)}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> falls below a tolerance (e.g. <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Because <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathrm{Id}}+\epsilon\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric positive definite,
CG converges rapidly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This iterative scheme is memory-efficient, requiring only matrix–vector products with
<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, and avoids the explicit computation of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, making it suitable for large-scale inverse problems and long video sequences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Spatio-temporal TV<sub id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_sub">3</sub> proximal (PDHG).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the regularised subproblem (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In A.2 Implementation of Likelihood Proximal Steps ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), we solve</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{{\bm{u}}}\;\underbrace{\tfrac{1}{2\sigma_{n}^{2}}\|\mathcal{A}{\bm{u}}-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|{\bm{u}}-\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}\|_{2}^{2}}_{f({\bm{u}})}\;+\;\underbrace{\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})}_{g(D_{\lambda}{\bm{u}})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>𝒖</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{{\bm{u}}}\;\underbrace{\tfrac{1}{2\sigma_{n}^{2}}\|\mathcal{A}{\bm{u}}-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|{\bm{u}}-\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}\|_{2}^{2}}_{f({\bm{u}})}\;+\;\underbrace{\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})}_{g(D_{\lambda}{\bm{u}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})\;=\;\mathrm{TV}_{3,\lambda}({\bm{u}})\;:=\;\sum_{\tau,c,i,j}\sqrt{\,\lambda_{h}^{2}\big(D_{h}{\bm{u}}_{\tau,c,i,j}\big)^{2}+\lambda_{v}^{2}\big(D_{v}{\bm{u}}_{\tau,c,i,j}\big)^{2}+\lambda_{t}^{2}\big(D_{\tau}{\bm{u}}_{\tau,c,i,j}\big)^{2}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>TV</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\lambda}({\bm{u}})\;=\;\mathrm{TV}_{3,\lambda}({\bm{u}})\;:=\;\sum_{\tau,c,i,j}\sqrt{\,\lambda_{h}^{2}\big(D_{h}{\bm{u}}_{\tau,c,i,j}\big)^{2}+\lambda_{v}^{2}\big(D_{v}{\bm{u}}_{\tau,c,i,j}\big)^{2}+\lambda_{t}^{2}\big(D_{\tau}{\bm{u}}_{\tau,c,i,j}\big)^{2}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}:=\bigl[\,\lambda_{h}D_{h},\;\lambda_{v}D_{v},\;\lambda_{\tau}D_{\tau}\,\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}:=\bigl[\,\lambda_{h}D_{h},\;\lambda_{v}D_{v},\;\lambda_{\tau}D_{\tau}\,\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(D_{\lambda}{\bm{u}})=\|D_{\lambda}{\bm{u}}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(D_{\lambda}{\bm{u}})=\|D_{\lambda}{\bm{u}}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The associated subproblem in (<a href="#A1.E10" title="In Spatio-temporal TV3 proximal (PDHG). ‣ A.2 Implementation of Likelihood Proximal Steps ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) is convex and can be solved using the
<em id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">primal–dual hybrid gradient</em> (PDHG, Chambolle–Pock) algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chambolle &amp; Pock (2011)</a></cite>.
Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{p}}=(p_{h},p_{v},p_{\tau})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{p}}=(p_{h},p_{v},p_{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the dual variable with three components per voxel.
Given stepsizes <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho,\sigma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho,\sigma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\sigma\|D_{\lambda}\|^{2}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\sigma\|D_{\lambda}\|^{2}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and extrapolation <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, the iterations read:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{p}}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{p}}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{prox}_{\sigma g^{\ast}}\!\bigl({\bm{p}}^{k}+\sigma D_{\lambda}\bar{{\bm{u}}}^{k}\bigr)=\frac{{\bm{p}}^{k}+\sigma D_{\lambda}\bar{{\bm{u}}}^{k}}{\max\!\bigl(1,\;\|{\bm{p}}^{k}+\sigma D_{\lambda}\bar{{\bm{u}}}^{k}\|_{2}\bigr)}\quad\text{(projection onto unit $\ell_{2}$ ball)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mtext>(projection onto unit </mtext><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mtext> ball)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{prox}_{\sigma g^{\ast}}\!\bigl({\bm{p}}^{k}+\sigma D_{\lambda}\bar{{\bm{u}}}^{k}\bigr)=\frac{{\bm{p}}^{k}+\sigma D_{\lambda}\bar{{\bm{u}}}^{k}}{\max\!\bigl(1,\;\|{\bm{p}}^{k}+\sigma D_{\lambda}\bar{{\bm{u}}}^{k}\|_{2}\bigr)}\quad\text{(projection onto unit $\ell_{2}$ ball)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{u}}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{u}}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{prox}_{\rho f}\bigl({\bm{u}}^{k}-\rho D_{\lambda}^{\top}{\bm{p}}^{k+1}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{prox}_{\rho f}\bigl({\bm{u}}^{k}-\rho D_{\lambda}^{\top}{\bm{p}}^{k+1}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\text{obtained by solving }\bigl(I+\rho(\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}+\tfrac{1}{\delta\eta}I)\bigr){\bm{u}}^{k+1}={\bm{z}}+\rho\Bigl(\mathcal{A}^{\top}{\bm{y}}+\tfrac{1}{\delta\eta}\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}\Bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>obtained by solving </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\text{obtained by solving }\bigl(I+\rho(\mathcal{A}^{\top}\mathcal{A}+\tfrac{1}{\delta\eta}I)\bigr){\bm{u}}^{k+1}={\bm{z}}+\rho\Bigl(\mathcal{A}^{\top}{\bm{y}}+\tfrac{1}{\delta\eta}\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}\Bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\text{with }{\bm{z}}={\bm{u}}^{k}-\rho D_{\lambda}^{\top}{\bm{p}}^{k+1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒑</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\text{with }{\bm{z}}={\bm{u}}^{k}-\rho D_{\lambda}^{\top}{\bm{p}}^{k+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{{\bm{u}}}^{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{{\bm{u}}}^{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{u}}^{k+1}+\theta({\bm{u}}^{k+1}-{\bm{u}}^{k})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{u}}^{k+1}+\theta({\bm{u}}^{k+1}-{\bm{u}}^{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\lambda}^{\top}{\bm{p}}=\lambda_{h}D_{h}^{\top}p_{h}+\lambda_{v}D_{v}^{\top}p_{v}+\lambda_{\tau}D_{\tau}^{\top}p_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\lambda}^{\top}{\bm{p}}=\lambda_{h}D_{h}^{\top}p_{h}+\lambda_{v}D_{v}^{\top}p_{v}+\lambda_{\tau}D_{\tau}^{\top}p_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> is the weighted divergence, and
the proximal step for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f({\bm{u}})=\tfrac{1}{2\sigma_{n}^{2}}\|\mathcal{A}{\bm{u}}-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|{\bm{u}}-\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+1/4}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f({\bm{u}})=\tfrac{1}{2\sigma_{n}^{2}}\|\mathcal{A}{\bm{u}}-{\bm{y}}\|_{2}^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|{\bm{u}}-\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+1/4}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is implemented by solving the normal equations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">As in our implementation <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is often <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, to simplify the computations we remove the regularization term <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|{\bm{u}}-\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><mn mathsize="0.710em">4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2\delta\eta}\|{\bm{u}}-\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{k+\nicefrac{{1}}{{4}}}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Around <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> iterations of the CG algorithm can be used to solve the normal equations, as they are warm-started with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, we apply Chambolle–Pock (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 200</annotation></semantics></math> iterations) only in the <em id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">pure temporal TV</em> case (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{h}=\lambda_{v}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{h}=\lambda_{v}=0</annotation></semantics></math>).
When spatial weights are nonzero (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{h}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{h}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{v}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{v}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), we instead minimise (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In A.2 Implementation of Likelihood Proximal Steps ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) directly with <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Adam</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma &amp; Ba, 2014</a>)</cite> (learning rate <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> iterations), which proved more robust in this setting.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>The LATINO algorithm</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to clarify the practical implementation of the splitting scheme introduced in Equation (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In Zero-shot (plug &amp; play) posteror sampling. ‣ 2 Background ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), we provide here the pseudo-code to implement LATINO as described in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Spagnoletti et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> LATINO</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">given</span> <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}=\mathcal{A}^{\dagger}{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}=\mathcal{A}^{\dagger}{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, text prompt <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, number of steps <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, latent consistency model <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, latent space decoder <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, latent space encoder <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, sequences <math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{k},\delta_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{k},\delta_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,\ldots,N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,\ldots,N-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\text{Id})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>Id</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\text{Id})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t_{k}}^{(k)}\leftarrow\sqrt{\alpha_{t_{k}}}{\mathcal{E}}({\bm{x}}_{k})+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t_{k}}}\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t_{k}}^{(k)}\leftarrow\sqrt{\alpha_{t_{k}}}{\mathcal{E}}({\bm{x}}_{k})+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t_{k}}}\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Encode
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}^{(k)}\leftarrow{\mathcal{D}}(f_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{t_{k}}^{(k)},t_{k},c))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}^{(k)}\leftarrow{\mathcal{D}}(f_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{t_{k}}^{(k)},t_{k},c))</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Decode
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{k+1}\leftarrow\operatorname{prox}_{\delta_{k}g_{y}}({\bm{u}}^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{k+1}\leftarrow\operatorname{prox}_{\delta_{k}g_{y}}({\bm{u}}^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{{\bm{y}}}:{\bm{x}}\mapsto-\log p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{{\bm{y}}}:{\bm{x}}\mapsto-\log p({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>The Vision-XL algorithm</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">VISION-XL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon &amp; Ye (2025b)</a></cite> (Video Inverse-problem Solver using latent diffusION models) is a SOTA framework for high-resolution video inverse problems, LDMs such as SDXL to restore videos from measurements affected by spatio-temporal degradations.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Components</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">VISION-XL integrates three main contributions:
(i) <em id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Pseudo-batch inversion</em>, which initializes the sampling process from latents obtained by DDIM-inverting the measurement frames.
(ii) <em id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Pseudo-batch sampling</em>, which splits latent video frames and samples them in parallel using Tweedie’s formula <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Efron (2011)</a></cite>, reducing memory requirements to that of a single frame.
(iii) <em id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Pixel-space data-consistency updates</em>, where each denoised batch <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is refined using <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> iterations of a quadratic proximal step</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{t}=\arg\min_{{\bm{x}}\in\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{t}+K_{l}}\|{\bm{y}}-\mathcal{A}({\bm{x}})\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{t}=\arg\min_{{\bm{x}}\in\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{t}+K_{l}}\|{\bm{y}}-\mathcal{A}({\bm{x}})\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">typically solved via conjugate gradient (CG). This enforces alignment with the measurement before re-encoding to the latent space and re-noising for the next step.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Overall Algorithm.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Starting from <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{\rho}=\mathrm{DDIM}^{-1}(E_{\theta}({\bm{y}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>DDIM</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{\rho}=\mathrm{DDIM}^{-1}(E_{\theta}({\bm{y}}))</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\approx 0.3T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\approx 0.3T</annotation></semantics></math>, VISION-XL alternates denoising in latent space and proximal data-consistency refinement in pixel space. After decoding the denoised latent batch <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{t}=D_{\theta}(\hat{{\bm{z}}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{t}=D_{\theta}(\hat{{\bm{z}}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, a low-pass filter is applied to suppress high-frequency inconsistencies before re-encoding and re-noising, yielding <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. This process is repeated until <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, as shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ Overall Algorithm. ‣ A.4 The Vision-XL algorithm ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ L A TINO: LAtent Video consisTency INverse sOlver for High Definition Video Restoration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> VISION-XL</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
                
                
              Pretrained VAE encoder <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, decoder <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoiser <math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{(t)}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{(t)}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>,
measurement <math id="alg3.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, forward operator <math id="alg3.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial DDIM inversion step <math id="alg3.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>,
CG iterations <math id="alg3.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, low-pass filter widths <math id="alg3.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, noise schedule <math id="alg3.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bar{\alpha}_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bar{\alpha}_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
                
                
              <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{0}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}_{\theta}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{0}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}_{\theta}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
                
                
              <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{\rho}\leftarrow\mathrm{DDIM}^{-1}({\bm{z}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>DDIM</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{\rho}\leftarrow\mathrm{DDIM}^{-1}({\bm{z}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l3.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Step 1: <span id="alg3.l3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pseudo-batch inversion</span> (informative latent initialization)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
                
                
              <span id="alg3.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\rho,\ldots,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\rho,\ldots,2</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{z}}}_{t}\leftarrow\dfrac{{\bm{z}}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\,E^{(t)}_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{t})}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{z}}}_{t}\leftarrow\dfrac{{\bm{z}}_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\,E^{(t)}_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{t})}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg3.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Step 2: <span id="alg3.l5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pseudo-batch sampling</span> (Tweedie’s formula)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{t}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\theta}(\hat{{\bm{z}}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{t}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\theta}(\hat{{\bm{z}}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
