<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Slice comparisons across two sequences. In <span id="A2.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00FF00;">green</span>, the sliced column. Slice images are obtained from the three-dimensional video tensor (i,j,<math id="A2.F7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>) by fixing a column index j. This leads to a 2D tensor with indices (i,<math id="A2.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>) that is represented as an image, where the i index represents the row and the t index represents the column.</figcaption>
</figure>
